<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://polyarchives.hosting.nyu.edu/items/show/542">
<dc:title>2001: A Space Odyssey - Videophone Sequence

</dc:title>
<dc:subject>Science Fiction; Videophone; Film Technology; Stanley Kubrick; &quot;2001: A Space Odyssey&quot;</dc:subject>
<dc:description>A clip from &quot;2001: A Space Odyssey&quot; demonstrating one of the earliest cinematic depictions of a videophone, showcasing director Stanley Kubrick&#039;s visionary portrayal of future technology. The sequence is noted for its prescient depiction of communication technology.</dc:description>
<dc:creator>Stanley Kubrick (Director)</dc:creator>
<dc:source>YouTube Channel - imaucblog</dc:source>
<dc:publisher>Warner Bros., Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer, United Artists</dc:publisher>
<dc:date>Original release date of the movie: April 2, 1968; YouTube clip posted on May 19, 2010</dc:date>
<dc:contributor>Keir Dullea (Actor portraying Dr. Dave Bowman), Arthur C. Clarke (Author of the original story), Geoffrey Unsworth, John Alcott (Cinematographers)</dc:contributor>
<dc:rights>The rights to the clip and the film are owned by the distributors: Warner Bros., Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer, United Artists. The clip is used for educational or critical commentary purposes, potentially covered under fair use.</dc:rights>
<dc:relation>Related to the broader context of &quot;2001: A Space Odyssey&quot; and its influence on science fiction and technology.

</dc:relation>
<dc:format>Video clip; Digital</dc:format>
<dc:language>English</dc:language>
<dc:type>Film excerpt; Cinematic depiction</dc:type>
<dc:identifier>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vWwo6JpMceg</dc:identifier>
<dc:coverage>The videophone sequence specifically covers future communication technologies as envisioned in a 1968 science fiction film.</dc:coverage>
</rdf:Description>
